# What the Docker build does NOT need to see.
#
# The image is built from exactly three things — package.json (+ lock),
# server/ and public/. Everything else is noise, and some of it is heavy:
# sending the whole directory as build context made every `up --build`
# upload a few hundred MB before the first instruction ran.
node_modules
data
pgdata
*.log
.DS_Store

# Secrets and local overrides are never part of an image.
.env
.env.*

# Local databases, dumps and backups.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
/*.sql
*.sql.gz
*.dump
*.backup
backups

# Agent transcripts and task logs: 260 MB of them, and they quote session
# cookies and demo passwords. Also excluded from git (.gitignore).
.pi

# Docker/compose/git plumbing itself.
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore
.gitignore
.git
README.md
.vscode
.idea
